## Exceptions -- third-party files NOT covered by the MIT license above

The MIT license applies only to this project's own source code (C, Python,
assembly, build scripts, docs). It does NOT apply to, and makes no claim
of ownership over, the following third-party files, which retain their
own original copyrights and are included here for development/testing
purposes only:

- **`roms/*.zip`** (`apple2e.zip`, `a2diskiing.zip`, `d2fdc.zip`,
  `votrsc01a.zip`) -- Apple IIe and Disk II controller system firmware ROM
  images. These are copyrighted Apple Computer, Inc. firmware. Files of
  this kind are widely archived at [archive.org](https://archive.org)'s
  software libraries; for convenience during this development session
  they were actually fetched from the MAME-compatible ROM set collection
  maintained at [Abdess/retrobios](https://github.com/Abdess/retrobios)
  (GitHub) rather than archive.org directly. Not redistributable under
  this project's license; included only to support local MAME-based
  development/verification testing (see `tools/README_oregon_trail.md`
  and `tools/mame_dump_memory.lua`).

- **`tools/assets/oregon_trail_title.png`** -- a screenshot of the
  original 1985 *The Oregon Trail* (MECC) Apple II title screen. Screenshots
  of this game are widely archived at [archive.org](https://archive.org)'s
  software library; for convenience this specific file was actually
  fetched from [MobyGames](https://www.mobygames.com/)'s CDN
  (`cdn.mobygames.com`) rather than archive.org directly. Used here for
  development/testing purposes (Hi-Res bitmap conversion pipeline
  verification) under fair-use/reference norms; not an original work of
  this project and not covered by the MIT license above.

If you're redistributing this repository, exclude or replace the files
listed above -- they are not licensed for redistribution by this project.

Everything else in this repository (all `.c`/`.h`/`.s`/`.py`/`.md`/`.dsk`
files not listed above, including the synthetic disk images in `disks/`,
which are generated entirely by this project's own tools, not copied from
any external source) is covered by the MIT license above.
